      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{618aa66840556f253acb7b2a|full_name}: That is because it wipe also stored settings by removing app. VRChat app is still same.\nI checked today which part is the problem... and it was local avatar settings. The settings seems not more compatible with new patches lately and broke the avatar loading / calibration, caused by wrong avatar settings.\nWhen i wiped the local avatar settings (can done in Settings -> Advanced Settings -> Clear Local Avatar data) and checked it, now all avatars loaded normal.\nReinstall app is not needed, just wipe data and it fixed the problem.\nStill, the app updates should recover it from incorrect avatar data or ignore it. It seems app code has not some extra checks to avoid problems by incompatible avatar data after some patches.\nPlease make sure it won't happens again, dear developers.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-02T17:55:05.234Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "World load problem: some worlds takes almost forever and will cause in the end time out connection. After some load tries, world loaded finally.\nHappens more often in bigger worlds, but also sometimes in small worlds. This is kinda annoying problem.\nAlso, world initialization is very long in most cases. What is going on there in 1170 version for Quest side.\nSecond problem is even more serious, maybe due OSC in Quest. I noticed the calibration step has weird behaviour. It goes in ON-OFF effect.\nIt means if you try change to other avatar, it will see broken (and doesn't not show in mirror) stays in arms-down position.\nGet another avatar, it's back to normal (mean calibration step is done).\nBUT if you change again, it's in wrong position again. So you must load again another avatar to restore it.\nReload world will activate re-calibration too, but also i saw ON-OFF effect. Means if you're good and go to other world, you will show in broken state. Reload world again recovers again to normal state.\nBut due ON-OFF bug effect, this is extremely annoying bug and will affect to pretty much ALL Quest users!!!!!!!!! Yes, it affects thousands users already this problem.\nSee the video as proof. Extremely annoying bug, it must fixed ASAP!\n\nVideo as proof: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LZOkrzwKwDM",
